        "original_id": "5e3d8708-2577-5d18-bd80-06eb57fd68cc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Schuyler, A. E. Housman, John Ashbery, Kenneth Koch\n- Organizations: Locus Solus\n- Works: A Shropshire Lad, On Wenlock Edge\n- Topics: poetry, classical scholarship, song cycles, literary magazines\n\nFacts:\n- A. E. Housman's 1896 collection \"A Shropshire Lad\" is the source of the six poems used in the song cycle \"On Wenlock Edge\".\n- A. E. Housman, born Alfred Edward Housman (26 March 1859 – 30 April 1936), was an English classical scholar and poet best known to the general public for \"A Shropshire Lad\".\n- James Marcus Schuyler (November 9, 1923 – April 12, 1991) was an American poet.\n- The magazine Locus Solus was edited by the poets John Ashbery, Kenneth Koch, and James Schuyler, and all three contributed to its four issues.",
